trality error, none 0.083, green 0.089, mid 0.088, among those whose kodak_portra_endura neutral filters fall in the shipped films' range), densitometer normalisation. Then Negs's steps: sensitivity scaled so an 18.4 % grey gives raw exposure 1 per channel under the reference illuminant, and spektrafilm's grey-ramp refinement run on spektrafilm 28bf883 through kodak_portra_endura at data_trustability 0.3. hanatos2025 adaptation window [445.7, 22.7, 595.5, 49.5] fitted on the reflectance corpus (Otsu (https://github.com/enneract/otsu2018), Munsell (https://zenodo.org/records/3269912), human skin (https://www.nist.gov/programs-projects/reflectance-measurements-human-skin), forest colors (https://zenodo.org/records/3269920)) with a weak prior toward the median of spektrafilm's stored windows. Tools and procedure: tools/film_profiles, docs/adding-film-stocks.md.\nNegs choices: reference illuminant D55 (daylight stock, exposed at 5400 K); viewing illuminant D50; target print kodak_portra_endura; log_sensitivity_density_over_min 1.0 as printed; spectra left empty (null) outside the published wavelength range; characteristic curves in log10 H as printed; use 'still' and antihalation 'weak' as the shipped still portrait negatives (Kodak Portra 160, Fujifilm Pro 160S).\nNote: Negs has no Konica QA RA-4 print paper; refined against kodak_portra_endura as the portrait RA-4 reference paper.\nNote: The 4-page 2004 brochure prints no RMS granularity; diffuse RMS granularity 4 (48 um aperture, D 1.0) is cross-verified from fresh-era datasheet compilations (cacreeks.com/films.htm and foto-35mm.narod.ru, matching Konica Centuria 100/200/400 = 4).\nRelative axes: sensitivity y axis: Relative Speed (log) carries a 1.0 scale bar between the two horizontal gridlines and no tick values; the offset is arbitrary and D5 rescales every channel.","referenceIlluminant":"D55","densitometer":"status_M","densityMinimum":[0.182,0.518,0.794],"wavelengths":[380,385,390,395,400,405,410,415,420,425,43